SUMMARY:Connecticut: CT-1065/CT-1120SI extended due date
DESCRIPTION:Extended due date\, via File Form CT-1065/CT-1120SI EXT for an 
 automatic 6-month extension.. | Connecticut partnership/S-corp composite re
 turn due the 15th day of the 3rd month after year-end. Connecticut's PE Tax
  (elective as of 2024) is reported on this same return series. File Form CT
 -1065/CT-1120SI EXT for an automatic 6-month extension. Correction (this re
 build session): the cited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3
 rd month) without addressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 
 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with every other state in this data set t
 hat explicitly confirms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New Yo
 rk\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16
 \, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US government-deadline convention of
  shifting to the next business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected f
 rom an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed app
 lication of the general shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched 
 per-state confirmation that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged 
 here for transparency. | Authority: Connecticut Department of Revenue Servi
 ces\, direct fetch this session: "on or before the fifteenth day of the thi
 rd month following the close of the taxable year"\; extension form confirms
  "a six-month extension of time to file Form CT-1065/CT-1120SI." | Source: 
 https://portal.ct.gov/drs/taxes/pass-through-entity/tax-information | This 
 date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announc
 ed change\; confirm against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
